      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Tilting the machine is a drastic measure, and you should try to avoid that unless absolutely necessary, as it can cause more trouble than it solves. The leak sensor, or float switch, is usually located in the bottom sump area, often near the drain pump. To access it, you'll likely need to remove the kick panels at the front of the dishwasher to get a better view underneath. Once you have access, carefully inspect the sensor for any visible debris or sludge that might be preventing it from reading correctly.",
